$DIR/test.p:88:49: packed fields need 10 bits but the backing type uint8 holds 8
    The fields of a packed type are laid out one after another, from bit 0.
    Their widths add up to more bits than the backing type holds.
    Use a larger backing type, make fields narrower, or leave the backing type
    out so the size follows the fields.
    (see "packed types" in the Plutonium spec, section 7.14)
    (run "pluto explain E2102" for a longer explanation)
